bms-bridge (2.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Daily energy aggregation: new daily_energy table accumulates charged/
    discharged kWh per battery per day; raw samples older than 8 days are
    purged automatically (migration runs on first start).
  * New /daily API endpoint for per-battery monthly energy data.
  * New Energy tab: monthly bar chart (charged/discharged kWh) with
    prev/next month navigation, per-battery selector, monthly totals.
  * Realtime tab: power in kW displayed alongside current reading.
  * Legacy battery labelled "Archive" across all charts and selectors.

 -- Alexey Volokitin <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Wed, 20 May 2026 11:00:00 +0300

bms-bridge (1.9.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Reserve battery: SoC%, voltage, cells and temps now mirror the monitored
    battery. Capacity fields use the reserve's own configured Ah but scale
    remaining by the mirror's SoC%. Current stays 0 A; charge/discharge
    limit stays 0.5C of the reserve's own capacity.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Mon, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bms-bridge (1.8.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * BLE scan coordinator: serialise the scan+connect phase across all BLE
    batteries sharing the one HCI adapter (FIFO slot, held only during
    scan/connect, released once the GATT connection is up or on backoff).
    No behaviour change with a single BLE battery.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Mon, 18 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bms-bridge (1.7.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Multi-battery support
  * History: one shared DB, legacy pre-multi-battery rows kept under the
    empty battery id. DB schema migration runs idempotently from postinst;
    no migration in the binary.
  * History read path: separate read-only SQLite connection; decimated
    /history query rewritten with a window function (~75 s → ~30 ms).
  * Pylontech master: bridge polls a `ttl`/`pylontech` battery over UART
  * Inverter exposes each battery as its own contiguous Pylontech module
    range (by configured capacity); reserve battery mirrors a sibling
    (SoC 100 %, 0 A, 0.5C limits).
  * UART transport: serial read()==0 is no-data, not a disconnect.
  * Dashboard: history charts moved to vendored Chart.js; per-battery
    selector for Realtime/Settings; history shows one line per battery.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Mon, 18 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

