bms-bridge (1.5.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Dashboard: full rewrite with Alpine.js, three tabs (Realtime/Settings/History),
    semi-circular gauges for voltage and current, SoC bar, live cell voltages grid,
    auto-refresh every 500 ms, history auto-reload at one-point-interval cadence.
  * HTTP: static file serving from www_root with MIME detection and path-traversal
    protection; new `/info` endpoint returning JkSettings as JSON; `/` redirects to
    index.html
  * Protocol fix: balancer_enabled was read from wrong frame offset (169); corrected
    to offset 140+telem_shift.
  * New field: balance_current_ma parsed from frame offset 138+telem_shift, stored
    in SQLite (migration), returned in /history JSON and shown in the Realtime
    status strip.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Wed, 06 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bms-bridge (1.4.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Refactor: BMS frame handling extracted from main() into BmsHandler class
    with named methods (on_queue_event, on_poll_tick, on_settings_tick,
    on_cell_info, on_device_info, on_settings_frame).
  * Config: BLE UUIDs now optional with standard JK BMS defaults; pylontech
    RS485 base address hardcoded to 2 (Pylontech convention); all optional
    parameters commented out in the config template.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Mon, 05 May 2026 15:00:00 +0000

bms-bridge (1.3.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * HTTP server: fix evthread_use_pthreads for correct cross-thread shutdown;
    serve dashboard HTML from configurable www_root; server-side decimation
    (step_ms = window/count) so any time window returns exactly count points;
    stale pagination contexts evicted after 5 min.
  * Dashboard: voltage, current, SoC and temperature charts, dark theme,
    time-range selector (1h/6h/24h/7d), hover tooltip.
  * Throttle history writes to once per bms_poll_period_ms and SharedState
    updates to once per bms_state_update_interval_ms (default 500 ms) to
    reduce dispatcher load from unsolicited JK BLE pushes (~2.4 fps).

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Mon, 05 May 2026 14:00:00 +0000

bms-bridge (1.2.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * HTTP server (default port 8080) serving a
    placeholder HTML page at / and paginated telemetry history at
    /history. Pagination via ?next&req_id=<uuid4>; time window and
    record count are configurable per request (defaults: last 24 h,
    100 records newest-first). http_port configurable in bms_bridge.conf.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Mon, 05 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

bms-bridge (1.1.0) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Telemetry history: every cell_info sample is appended to a SQLite
    file (default /var/lib/bms_bridge/history.sqlite3, configurable
    via history_db_path or -d). Last 24 h are also kept in RAM for
    fast access from the upcoming HTTP graph endpoint. Schema is
    normalised: samples + sample_cells with FK / WITHOUT ROWID.
  * Dropped the inverter thread; UART now lives on the main
    dispatcher's epoll loop.

 -- alexey <elenaluk89@gmail.com>  Mon, 04 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

